  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a permutation array AAA of integers in the range [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nYour task is to handle QQQ queries of the following type:\n\n\nGiven LLL and RRR, first create a new array BBB, also of length NNN, according to the following:\n\nBi=LB_i = LBi​=L if Ai&lt;LA_i &lt; LAi​&lt;L.\nBi=AiB_i = A_iBi​=Ai​ if L≤Ai≤RL \\le A_i \\le RL≤Ai​≤R\nBi=RB_i = RBi​=R if R&lt;AiR &lt; A_iR&lt;Ai​.\n\n\nFind the number of inversions†^{\\dagger}† in BBB.\n†^{\\dagger}† An inversion is a pair (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i &lt; j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N and Bi&gt;BjB_i &gt; B_jBi​&gt;Bj​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN and QQQ - the size of the array and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the array.\nThe next QQQ lines contain 222 integers each - LLL and RRR, the parameters for each query.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, output on a new line the number of inversions in the constructed array BBB.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\le A_i \\le N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "Ai≠AjA_i \\ne A_jAi​=Aj​ when i≠ji \\ne ji=j",
      "1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
